Lightningpanda patch 0030: the first VM of a process does not ask for the main bundle or list ICU's time zones.

The first `JSContextGroupCreate` of a process took 5.1 ms on an M1 Max (C harness, static
library); two things were 3.4 ms of it, and a command line browser needs neither at start:

- `TZoneHeapManager::init` seeds its key with the process name, which `ProcessCheck.mm` took from
  `[[NSBundle mainBundle] bundleIdentifier]` and `[[NSProcessInfo processInfo] processName]`: the
  main bundle lookup alone was 1.3 ms and more of CoreFoundation work (4.5 ms on a cold run). The
  name now comes from `getprogname()`, and the bundle identifier is not asked for: Gigacage's
  opt-in list (`jsc`, `test*`, ...) is matched against the same program name as before, and a
  command line embedder has no bundle identifier. Darwin only: other ports never had this file.

- `VM::VM` called `initializeAvailableTimeZones()`, which enumerates ICU's time zones twice and
  resolves each to its IANA primary: 2.2 ms. `utcTimeZoneID()` has had a slow path behind a
  `std::call_once` all along, so the first Intl or Temporal use of a zone builds the table.
  `JSPrepareTimeZones()` (JSForkPrivate.h) builds it on demand, on any thread: a process that
  forks its pages calls it once, beside engine creation, so that no page builds it again.

First `JSContextGroupCreate`: 5.1 -> 1.7 ms.

